From 195ace3eb8a521950c72ffc62f0349aed6c7ac04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 22:51:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 142/258] feat(cuda): add native W8A8 dp4a integer kernel plane
 (C6/R6)

Implement contract 0002 C6 / R6 for the CUDA backend as a separate,
probe-gated integer plane next to the unchanged float/bf16 PTX target:

- qmatmul_s8s8_s32 emits a native dp4a.s32.s32 main loop (SASS
  IDP.4A.S8.S8 on sm_120) with an explicit widening K tail
  (cvt.s32.s8 + mad.lo.s32); rank2/3/4, identical batch prefixes,
  K <= 133144 and reserved -128 handling match the C1 scalar golden.
- quantize_per_token_s8, dequantize_s8 and
  dequantize_epilogue_bf16 are native target entry points bit-exact
  with the C1 goldens (Q1-Q6): per-row absmax, double-precision ratio
  with cvt.rni RNE, clamp/saturation count, explicit integer bf16 RNE,
  NaN/Inf, scale underflow and binary32 overflow fail closed.
- the capability declaration is a CapabilitySet (dtypes int8/int32/
  float32/bf16, matrix kind s8s8_s32_dp4a); the real Driver API probe
  derives dp4a (sm>=61) and reports imma (sm>=75) without claiming it.
  Nothing hardcodes sm_120; a missing driver or an insufficient device
  fails closed with UnsupportedCapabilityError, never a BF16 fallback.
- three-layer artifact gate: payload version 3 (the float CUDA plane
  stays at 2), the pypto-x.cuda.w8a8:1 marker in PTX and metadata, and
  kernel version 1; every decode re-renders the PTX, recomputes all
  digests and re-probes the device/capability digest, so old payloads,
  tampered metadata and cross-plane artifacts fail closed.
- 56 focused tests cover the four opcodes against the portable golden
  through a deterministic fake driver, PTX structure/marker checks,
  capability gating (sm_50/60/70/74 injected), K over-limit, zero-size
  rejection, -128 rejection and artifact tampering.
- cuda_w8a8_device_validation.py is a weight-free RTX 5080 driver: the
  first run exposed two PTX address bugs (qmatmul tail right offset and
  the quantize codes row base) that the fake-driver contract tests
  could not see; both are fixed, pinned by a PTX-text regression test,
  and the final real-device run reports 53 checks / 0 mismatch.
- no model-level precision='w8a8-linear' path, no graph-contract change
  and no cuda.py (BF16) modification; AMD static lowering is not part of
  this commit (registered as not done in the evidence brief).
